WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.740
Russia holds a 5th of Ukraine, and Washington floated trading Donbass for NATO. This is Omni View, episode 236. After that comes a halt to flights across the United States, a funding emergency in Sudan, and pension anger on Europe's streets, then a health ruling, a rocket test, Dakar's games, and a closer look at how a pension budget actually gets locked in. Ukrainian president Volodymyr Zelensky told reporters on Saturday,

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.680
the BBC reports that American negotiators put a new question to Kiev.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:39.140
Pull the forces still holding ground in the eastern Donbass and join the North Atlantic

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.880
Treaty Organization, or NATO.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:47.260
He said he would send any package to a referendum only if it carried security guarantees, no cap

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.740
on Ukraine's army, and money to rebuild.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.740
End-voys Jared Kushner and Steve Whitkov saw him in Dublin on Thursday after sitting with

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.980
with Russian president Vladimir Putin in Moscow the day before.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.840
The Moscow stop was already on this show.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:06.880
What is new is the trade itself, which he said had never been raised, and which made

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.460
him think a alliance membership was back on the agenda after US officials had taken it

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.120
off the table.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.560
He still called the talk with Putin extremely difficult.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.680
Moscow's published terms have included a smaller Ukrainian military, land handed over, and

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:22.880
guaranteed neutrality.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.880
Kiiv has rejected those as leaving it unable to stop another invasion, and Kremlin comments

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.640
suggest that list has not moved.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:36.840
France 24, using remarks his office released, puts the same American question after talks

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:42.300
in Abu Dhabi, rather than after Dublin, and quotes him warning that a Kremlin rewrite of

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:47.260
Europe's security setup leads to wars or escalations, and that real security in Europe

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.200
means the European Union and NATO.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.560
video. The BBC adds that giving up the sliver still held would be small on a map and large

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:59.800
as a symbol, because it would accept the Donbass as Russian, and that first lady Melania

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:05.640
Trump last month helped open a short ceasefire in occupied Oleshky so people in aid could move.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:11.440
His case is that a question is not a deal. Without guarantees, an unconstrained army and

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:16.380
rebuild funds, there is nothing he is willing to ask voters to weigh, because membership

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:23.400
is the deterrent against the next attack. Putin's stated case is that another alliance member on Russia's border is unacceptable,

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:28.820
and that neutrality plus a smaller force is what removes the threat Moscow says it is fighting.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:35.680
Zelensky marks the limit on his own reading himself. Putin's signals make the conversation extremely hard.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:42.220
The reports do not show Moscow giving any turn back. If a written package with those three pieces appears,

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:45.100
years, watch whether he actually puts it to a referendum.

00:02:46.057 --> 00:02:50.817
Civil air travel across the United States stopped on Friday when links between air traffic

00:02:50.817 --> 00:02:51.817
facilities failed.

00:02:52.477 --> 00:02:57.977
The Federal Aviation Administration, the agency that runs that airspace, saw aging radar

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:01.297
and telecom begin to falter at 336 in the afternoon.

00:03:01.977 --> 00:03:07.777
The New York Times reports, France 24 reports that more than 8,200 flights were cancelled,

00:03:07.777 --> 00:03:16.677
over 31% of the US schedule in a stop that lasted nearly five hours, the longest in the country since September 11th, 2001.

00:03:17.437 --> 00:03:20.737
Officials blamed old equipment and routers overloaded with data.

00:03:21.377 --> 00:03:23.857
The order is lifted and aircraft are moving again.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:28.997
Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said it would still take time to get back to capacity

00:03:28.997 --> 00:03:32.537
and that he expected a normal schedule by the Thanksgiving rush.

00:03:32.537 --> 00:03:37.217
The time says this was only the third nationwide ground stop the agency has

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:42.717
issued this century, and the second longest after the 2001 attacks. A shorter one

00:03:42.717 --> 00:03:48.357
followed a pilot alert outage on January 11, 2023. More than 1,000 aircraft

00:03:48.357 --> 00:03:52.917
were already in the air and headed for US airports while the stop was on. A

00:03:52.917 --> 00:03:57.097
typical day puts more than two million people through security checkpoints. On

00:03:57.097 --> 00:04:00.897
Thursday the Transportation Security Administration screened nearly two and a

00:04:00.897 --> 00:04:06.057
half-million. Homeland Security Secretary Mark Wayne Mullin said there was never an indication

00:04:06.057 --> 00:04:11.257
of a cyber attack, and that lives were never in danger, and he also said investigators

00:04:11.257 --> 00:04:16.517
were still looking and would not rule an attack out. France 24 reports officials said there

00:04:16.517 --> 00:04:22.417
was no evidence of one. Congress approved $12.5 billion last year to upgrade facilities

00:04:22.417 --> 00:04:27.877
and technology. A sum Duffy has called a down payment. On Friday night, he asked for another

00:04:27.877 --> 00:04:32.517
50 billion dollars in emergency money before the end of the year, up from a 30

00:04:32.517 --> 00:04:36.677
billion dollar request because he said control of Congress and the budget then

00:04:36.677 --> 00:04:41.077
switches from Republicans to Democrats. His argument is that the same old

00:04:41.077 --> 00:04:45.217
links will fail again unless that check arrives while his party still holds the

00:04:45.217 --> 00:04:49.737
budget. Some Democratic lawmakers have already asked whether the agency has

00:04:49.737 --> 00:04:53.917
spent what it already received efficiently. The articles do not quote them

00:04:53.917 --> 00:04:59.377
saying the current kit is fine. Watch whether that emergency sum is approved before the budget

00:04:59.377 --> 00:05:05.075
changes hands at the end of the year. Sudan's emergency stocks of shelter and basic household

00:05:05.075 --> 00:05:11.175
goods are running out. The international organization for migration and the UN Refugee Agency say,

00:05:11.655 --> 00:05:18.675
Deutscheweller reports, the United Nations plan needs $2.9 billion to reach 20.4 million people,

00:05:18.675 --> 00:05:25.295
and 47% of that money is in. 33.7 million people in the country depend on aid.

00:05:25.755 --> 00:05:32.195
15.4 million need shelter and household items. And agencies have been able to help only 10% of them.

00:05:32.815 --> 00:05:39.335
More than 3.5 years after war began between the Sudanese Armed Forces and the paramilitary rapid support forces.

00:05:39.895 --> 00:05:46.735
About 8.6 million people have fled inside the country. More than 4.6 million have crossed into neighboring states

00:05:46.735 --> 00:05:51.295
and another 5.2 million have gone back to towns that are already destroyed.

00:05:52.055 --> 00:05:55.495
Death estimates run from 40,000 to 250,000.

00:05:56.075 --> 00:06:00.535
Fresher counts are blocked by fighting, curbed satellite internet, and the departure of

00:06:00.535 --> 00:06:01.295
many observers.

00:06:01.955 --> 00:06:07.295
Marina Peter, who chairs the Sudan and South Sudan form in Germany, told Deutschewelle that

00:06:07.295 --> 00:06:12.675
some people have lived on routes, that rations and refugee camps have been cut sharply, and

00:06:12.675 --> 00:06:16.895
And that child mortality is above average while the armed party still obstruct access.

00:06:17.695 --> 00:06:22.535
Evil corner of Caritas International told the same outlet that the United States, Germany

00:06:22.535 --> 00:06:27.095
and the European Union are giving far less than they did four or five years ago.

00:06:27.815 --> 00:06:34.275
Caritas still provides cash, drinking water, basic medical care and seeds, but its 2026 projects

00:06:34.275 --> 00:06:36.795
in Sudan have been paid for only by donations.

00:06:36.795 --> 00:06:44.095
On October 23rd, the United Kingdom and 31 other partners, Germany among them, said 19.5

00:06:44.095 --> 00:06:49.295
million people, about 41% of the population, face acute food insecurity.

00:06:50.035 --> 00:06:54.475
Corner hopes for money from the German Foreign Office and expects the door to be narrower

00:06:54.475 --> 00:06:55.795
than in earlier years.

00:06:56.744 --> 00:06:59.664
Paris is due to see a fifth straight Saturday of marches.

00:07:00.224 --> 00:07:06.064
France 24 reports, with campaign groups, students, and yellow vest protesters joining demands

00:07:06.064 --> 00:07:09.024
hands on wages, education, and civil liberties.

00:07:09.664 --> 00:07:14.664
The Hindu reports that thousands of arrests, police beatings, and limits on marches have

00:07:14.664 --> 00:07:19.224
added to a swell that shows no sign of easing before next year's presidential election.

00:07:20.084 --> 00:07:25.464
The New York Times sets those marches and recent youth protests in Belgium, Germany, Greece,

00:07:25.864 --> 00:07:28.604
Italy, and Portugal against a budget fact.

00:07:28.944 --> 00:07:33.764
As Europeans live longer, pensions are routinely the largest lines in national budgets.

00:07:33.764 --> 00:07:39.664
units. Union leaders warned that fatigue is setting in. France 24 says, while officers

00:07:39.664 --> 00:07:44.424
want better pay for the risk of policing the streets. Many teachers back students who

00:07:44.424 --> 00:07:48.964
have blockaded high schools for nearly two months, and headteachers gathered on Friday

00:07:48.964 --> 00:07:55.184
saying threats and violence have become unbearable, and asking the state to protect them. Sebastian

00:07:55.184 --> 00:08:01.464
Ducro, a 36-year-old data analyst who supports the students, told the Times that dilapidated schools

00:08:01.464 --> 00:08:06.484
lose because a huge portion of the money goes to retirees, and that people like his parents

00:08:06.484 --> 00:08:09.524
about to retire could surrender some of their pension.

00:08:10.284 --> 00:08:16.264
Laurent Grindwald, 72, who retired after decades as a postal worker, told the times he is

00:08:16.264 --> 00:08:21.064
not eager to give any of it back for other services, especially with rents and living costs

00:08:21.064 --> 00:08:23.864
up, after a working life already paid in.

00:08:24.484 --> 00:08:30.224
Jorge Galindo, director of the Spanish think tank Assad-Eqpol, called the split a generational

00:08:30.224 --> 00:08:34.464
and noted that Spain has some of Europe's most generous pensions.

00:08:34.964 --> 00:08:37.544
Neither man is quoted accepting the others arithmetic.

00:08:38.715 --> 00:08:42.235
A regional health body has taken a status away from the United States

00:08:42.235 --> 00:08:44.655
that the country had held since 2000.

00:08:45.335 --> 00:08:49.135
The Pan American Health Organization revoked measles elimination status

00:08:49.135 --> 00:08:50.535
after 26 years.

00:08:51.135 --> 00:08:54.035
Deutscheweller reports citing a Wall Street Journal account

00:08:54.035 --> 00:08:55.875
of people familiar with the decision.

00:08:56.575 --> 00:09:00.375
A source close to the process told CNN that an independent commission

00:09:00.375 --> 00:09:05.075
reporting to the organization's director found the country no longer qualified.

00:09:05.575 --> 00:09:10.135
The test was whether one strain had circulated without a break for 12 months or more.

00:09:10.815 --> 00:09:15.695
A source familiar with the U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention findings told Reuters,

00:09:16.235 --> 00:09:18.975
the agency found 12 months of continuous spread.

00:09:19.655 --> 00:09:27.035
As of Thursday, the agency had recorded 5,182 confirmed cases across 45 states plus New

00:09:27.035 --> 00:09:28.615
York City and Washington, D.C.

00:09:28.615 --> 00:09:38.315
more than double 2025's 2,289. About 7,500 people have been infected and 13 have died since 2025.

00:09:39.195 --> 00:09:43.955
Nearly all of this year's cases are in people who were unvaccinated or who status is unknown,

00:09:44.515 --> 00:09:49.795
and roughly one in nine patients were hospitalized, CNN reported, citing the CDC.

00:09:50.695 --> 00:09:55.635
Noel Brewer, a University of North Carolina professor who chairs an independent measles panel

00:09:55.635 --> 00:10:01.175
hospital, and who presented that CDC report on Tuesday, told Reuters it is a fully preventable

00:10:01.175 --> 00:10:04.235
disease and unconscionable to have this amount of measles.

00:10:04.915 --> 00:10:10.475
Johns Hopkins epidemiologist William Moss told Reuters the lost damages America's reputation

00:10:10.475 --> 00:10:14.355
as a public health leader, and means large outbreaks will continue.

00:10:14.935 --> 00:10:20.535
The stretch has come with more vaccine hesitancy under Health Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr.,

00:10:20.535 --> 00:10:24.535
who for years has doubted measles vaccine safety without scientific proof.

00:10:24.535 --> 00:10:30.195
CDC director Erica Schwartz, before the decision, said the agency would keep working with

00:10:30.195 --> 00:10:31.835
states to encourage vaccination.

00:10:32.195 --> 00:10:37.455
A country gets the status back only after transmission ends, and it stays outbreak free

00:10:37.455 --> 00:10:38.575
for at least 12 months.

00:10:39.658 --> 00:10:46.138
SpaceX sent Starship up on a 15th test flight, France 24 reports, aiming to reach orbit and

00:10:46.138 --> 00:10:48.718
release 15 satellites for its Starlink network.

00:10:48.718 --> 00:10:54.018
Deutscheweller reports the plan was, for the first time, to catch and later reuse

00:10:54.018 --> 00:10:59.418
both stages of what the company calls the world's largest spaceship. The spacecraft continued

00:10:59.418 --> 00:11:05.678
into orbit, the booster, meant to return to the pad, did not. France 24 says it splashed

00:11:05.678 --> 00:11:11.098
down in the Gulf of Mexico minutes after liftoff. Deutscheweller says it exploded over that

00:11:11.098 --> 00:11:16.238
same water. Neither report includes wreckage images or a company statement that would settle

00:11:16.238 --> 00:11:21.038
which account the hardware matches. Both say the upper stage flew on and the booster

00:11:21.038 --> 00:11:26.000
was not brought home. Dakar is a piece of progress worth knowing. The summer

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.740
Youth Olympics there ended Friday after two weeks.

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:33.320
Deutscheweller reports, the first Olympic event an African country has hosted.

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:40.040
Nearly 2,700 young athletes contested 153 medal events in 25 sports.

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:45.760
African teams took a record medal hall and Senegal won an Olympic gold for the first time

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:49.560
with 136 Senegalese athletes on the start lists.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:53.040
China led with 18 golds, Japan took 11,

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:57.780
Russia 8, Egypt 6, and Ethiopia and Senegal 5 each.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:00.260
International Olympic Committee President

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:03.120
Kirstie Coventry said expectations had been exceeded

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:05.580
and praised what happens when a whole country

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:07.180
comes together for its young people.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.020
The hard edge is political.

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:11.920
Russian athletes competed under their own flag

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:13.900
for the first time at an Olympic event

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:17.660
since the full-scale invasion of Ukraine in February 2022.

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:21.260
Chile, Paraguay, and Thailand have confirmed bids

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:24.200
to host the next summer Uth Olympics in 2030.

00:12:25.221 --> 00:12:28.081
In brief, Microsoft said Saturday that an outage

00:12:28.081 --> 00:12:29.741
of its business and government apps

00:12:29.741 --> 00:12:33.041
began around 1725 UTC on Thursday

00:12:33.041 --> 00:12:37.001
and logged in more than 7.4 million down detector reports

00:12:37.001 --> 00:12:39.881
is over, with the company blaming servers

00:12:39.881 --> 00:12:42.141
and saying it knew of no outside interference.

00:12:42.141 --> 00:12:47.561
South Sudan has moved its first legislative and presidential elections from December 22,

00:12:47.761 --> 00:12:48.341
to February.

00:12:48.901 --> 00:12:53.301
After earlier delays, and the United Nations had warned a vote could set off widespread

00:12:53.301 --> 00:13:00.501
conflict, Delhi's air quality index hit 334 on Friday, a hazardous reading above Lahore's,

00:13:00.781 --> 00:13:03.961
which IQ Air ranked the most polluted major city that day.

00:13:04.461 --> 00:13:09.641
Hong Kong police commissioner Joe Chow-Yat Ming said artificial intelligence facial recognition

00:13:09.641 --> 00:13:15.081
action, goes live across the forces' camera network on Monday, including for masked faces.

00:13:15.721 --> 00:13:21.061
Nigeria's electoral chairman, Joe Ash Amupitan, said the commission is investigating voter

00:13:21.061 --> 00:13:25.961
register images believed to be artificially generated, and has opened a unit to watch

00:13:25.961 --> 00:13:32.361
those threats before the 2027 vote, with President Bola Tanubu facing Atiku Abu Bakar and

00:13:32.361 --> 00:13:33.081
Peter Obi.

00:13:33.741 --> 00:13:38.541
Chinese and US officials discussed tariffs and farm trade at a first-trade council meeting

00:13:38.541 --> 00:13:43.941
ahead of a G-Trump meeting. India's Prime Minister's Office summoned the telecom secretary

00:13:43.941 --> 00:13:49.421
over website takedowns that officials say used fake court orders. In Istanbul, police

00:13:49.421 --> 00:13:56.221
detained Heinrich Bell Foundation coordinator Jancha Verdeoglu Sik last Wednesday on an espionage

00:13:56.221 --> 00:14:02.601
accusation and released her under a travel ban. Her husband, lawmaker Amit Sik, said a state without

00:14:02.601 --> 00:14:08.461
law is a gang. The US military said drones over an American base in Britain drew a security

00:14:08.461 --> 00:14:14.361
response. UN health officials hailed six months of progress against Ebola and said the virus

00:14:14.361 --> 00:14:20.001
is still moving into more remote and dangerous parts of Congo. Advocates say immigrant families

00:14:20.001 --> 00:14:27.041
are being held in cold, sunless rooms past a 72-hour limit. Alan Milburn told the BBC that a legal

00:14:27.041 --> 00:14:32.961
guarantee of a job or training in a review due next week would mean some young people lose benefits.

00:14:32.961 --> 00:14:37.841
banks. Bank of England chief economist Hugh Pill told the Financial Times the bank

00:14:37.841 --> 00:14:43.701
is likely to raise rates further in 2027. Huge crowds and low vaccination rates are

00:14:43.701 --> 00:14:50.201
raising measles alarms as Pope Leo XIV visits South America. Hong Kong Home Affairs Secretary

00:14:50.201 --> 00:14:56.201
Alice Mack said the government will not immediately cap estate proxy votes and will trial electronic

00:14:56.201 --> 00:14:59.101
proxie voting next year after the Typo fire.

00:14:59.861 --> 00:15:05.901
And France 24, citing the Financial Times, says NVIDIA has approached arm chief Rene Hass

00:15:05.901 --> 00:15:09.121
as a possible successor after Jensen Huang resigned.

00:15:10.129 --> 00:15:14.849
To really understand the pension anger behind those European marches, look at the headcount,

00:15:15.109 --> 00:15:19.249
not the stereotype that the fight is only about whether older people have been too comfortable.

00:15:19.949 --> 00:15:26.189
Germany's public pension insurance had 3.73 contributors for every retiree in 1957.

00:15:26.189 --> 00:15:36.549
2021. By 2025, the ratio was 2.1. By 2045, it is projected at 1.73. 35.35 million contributors

00:15:36.549 --> 00:15:43.749
financing 16.82 million retirees. Deutscheweller reports in a data check on the generations. Holding

00:15:43.749 --> 00:15:49.329
contribution rates steady already costs about 118 billion euros a year in government subsidies.

00:15:49.909 --> 00:15:54.909
Roughly a quarter of the federal budget. So a rising share of everyone else's taxes is committed

00:15:54.909 --> 00:15:56.949
before schools or training are argued.

00:15:57.629 --> 00:16:03.009
Retirees on federal basic income support rose from 257,000 in 2003

00:16:03.009 --> 00:16:06.069
to 738,000 in 2024.

00:16:06.929 --> 00:16:11.209
Low income households spent about 24% of income on rent in 1990

00:16:11.209 --> 00:16:14.009
and nearly 36% in 2021.

00:16:14.809 --> 00:16:18.969
In 2025, 11% of the population spent more than 40%

00:16:18.969 --> 00:16:20.689
of disposable income on housing

00:16:20.689 --> 00:16:25.009
and among people at risk of poverty that share was 35%.

00:16:25.009 --> 00:16:31.229
Public education spending on people under 30 has doubled since 2011, from about 4,000

00:16:31.229 --> 00:16:37.949
euros to about 8,000 euros a person each year, and in 2022 it was still 4.6% of gross

00:16:37.949 --> 00:16:42.489
domestic product against an OECD average of 4.7%.

00:16:42.489 --> 00:16:48.629
Youth researcher Simon Schnitzer told Deutschewella that it is fair to ask whether earlier generations

00:16:48.629 --> 00:16:53.569
had it hard, and that young people are asking whether they have been given the conditions to live,

00:16:53.929 --> 00:16:59.509
work, and keep the system funded. A crowd report reads differently once you know the ratio and

00:16:59.509 --> 00:17:04.549
the subsidy share, because the argument is about what is already promised before this year's March

00:17:04.549 --> 00:17:11.089
starts. Next time, check whether the peace states that contributor to retiree ratio and the budget share

00:17:11.089 --> 00:17:18.059
or only describes the street. On the diplomacy, the BBC ties the Don Bass question to a Dublin meeting

00:17:18.059 --> 00:17:23.319
after Moscow notes that Washington had taken NATO membership off the table, while France

00:17:23.319 --> 00:17:29.359
24 ties it to Abu Dhabi, and adds Zelensky's line that only the European Union and NATO

00:17:29.359 --> 00:17:30.999
are real European security.

00:17:31.659 --> 00:17:33.419
That wraps up today's omnivue.

00:17:33.799 --> 00:17:38.779
Remember, the best informed people read more than one perspective, and the calmest ones

00:17:38.779 --> 00:17:42.359
know that most days, somewhere, something is quietly getting better.

